%% @fig 01
%% @kicker Price per million tokens, Q2 2026
%% @alt A horizontal bar chart of input and output prices per million tokens for seven models, from GPT-5.4 Nano at $0.20 input and $1.25 output to Claude Opus 4.7 at $5 input and $25 output. A table repeats the prices and shows that output costs 5 to 6.25 times input for every model listed.
%% @caption Prices from the article's Q2 2026 table, rounded to three significant figures. GPT-5.4 Pro ($30 / $180) is left out so the scale stays readable.
%% @series Input; Output
%% @unit $
%% @table Output premium | Model | Input | Output | Output ÷ input
%% @row GPT-5.4 Nano | $0.20 | $1.25 | 6.25×
%% @row GPT-5.4 Mini | $0.75 | $4.50 | 6×
%% @row Claude Haiku 4.5 | $1 | $5 | 5×
%% @row Gemini 3.1 Pro | $2 | $12 | 6×
%% @row GPT-5.4 Standard | $2.50 | $15 | 6×
%% @row Claude Sonnet 4.6 | $3 | $15 | 5×
%% @row Claude Opus 4.7 | $5 | $25 | 5×
%% @bar 2
xychart-beta horizontal
  x-axis ["GPT-5.4 Nano", "GPT-5.4 Mini", "Claude Haiku 4.5", "Gemini 3.1 Pro", "GPT-5.4 Standard", "Claude Sonnet 4.6", "Claude Opus 4.7"]
